WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:07.280
It's the job of law enforcement to have guns and to decide when to shoot.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:12.000
You just do not want the average citizen
carrying a gun in a crowded place.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.160
Former New York City Mayor Michael Bloomberg made that comment after an armed citizen

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.980
may have averted a mass shooting by
killing a gunman at a Texas church.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.640
It hasn't aged well.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:25.380
How convincing can Bloomberg's "only cops should have guns" message be

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:30.660
to Americans who have seen and shared fresh examples of unjustified and brutal police conduct?

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:34.620
Or who have witnessed scenes of rioters and looters putting their lives and property at risk

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.680
because law enforcement agencies failed to protect them?

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.880
The NYPD and the mayor did not do their job last night.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:46.720
A good many Americans took responsibility for their own safety, including people who fully support

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:51.440
protests against police misconduct, but see no reason to allow themselves to be victimized by hotheads

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:52.940
and opportunists.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:58.020
In St. Paul, Minnesota black residents stood armed guard against looters outside local businesses.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:00.620
Business owners in Kirkland, Washington did the same.

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:08.720
A Bellevue, Washington cigar shop owner chased off looters at gunpoint.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.760
They were acting in the tradition of the so-called "Roof Koreans,"

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:16.500
who defended their stores during the 1992 LA riots.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:20.660
I think one of his purposes is he wants potential looters to see it.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:25.040
I think he wants people, all of them up
there, they want people to see that they are armed

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.980
and that you enter their properties at some risk.

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:31.200
Many police departments conceded the limits of their
abilities.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:36.040
In Florida Sheriff Grady Judd advised Polk County residents to shoot looters.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:40.300
High-profile psychologist Scott Barry Kaufman, a gun control supporter, marveled on Twitter

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.760
that when he called Santa Monica Police over protests related confrontation,

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:47.220
they told him, "Sir the city is under attack. Do what you have to do."

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:51.320
For those who have been advising Americans for years that we should lay down our own weapons

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:54.960
and trust armed government employees to
protect us and treat us with respect

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.660
2020 has been a massive reality check.

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:00.080
The year so far has demonstrated, once again,

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:03.180
that the police can't be relied on to defend our lives and property,

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:04.900
and often pose threats themselves.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:12.280
It's the job of law enforcement to have guns and to decide when to shoot.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:16.100
If we were to follow the advice of those who would disarm us, we'd be even more at the mercy

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:19.700
of Derek Chauvin and his buddies, and anybody else with ill intent.

